Alembic migrations for ReckonAI. Single database, one linear history.

Two things differ from a stock Alembic setup, both deliberate:

  - The database URL is read from reckonai.config.Settings, not from
    alembic.ini, whose sqlalchemy.url is left empty. See env.py.
  - Migrations run on Render through the web service's preDeployCommand, never
    from a start command. See specs/2026-11-07-repo-deployment-skeleton
    requirements.md D7.

Because pre-deploy runs while the previous version is still serving traffic, a
migration must be backward compatible with the code it is replacing for the
length of the overlap window. Expand, then contract: add a column, deploy the
code that writes it, drop the old one in a later revision. Dropping or renaming
a column the running instance still selects will break it.

Usage:

  uv run alembic upgrade head
  uv run alembic downgrade base
  uv run alembic revision -m "<message>"
  uv run alembic upgrade head --sql      # review the SQL without connecting
